  <Place MSRCommunityId="0" MSRComponentId="0" Permission="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/eso/eso0421a/thumb.jpg" Name="The Orion Nebula (M42)" DataSetType="Sky" RA="5.5877739771288546" Dec="-5.3855261870959312" Constellation="ORI" Classification="Unidentified" Magnitude="0" Distance="0" ZoomLevel="5.48409093232197" Rotation="0" Angle="0" DomeAlt="0" DomeAz="0" Opacity="100" AngularSize="5.48409093232197">
    <Description> The individual images of the Orion Nebula where obtained with WFI at the ESO/MPG 2.2m telescope on the night of Dec.10-11, 2001. 
    Several images were obtained in the following filters: U (363.690 nm; 15 images for a total exposure time of 1.25 hour); B (456.252 nm; 14 images; 
    total exp.: 21 min); Oxygen [OIII] (502.393 nm; 15 images; total exp.: 32 min); Halpha (658.827 nm; 15 images; total exp.: 32 min); Sulphur [SII] 
    (676.340 nm; 10 images; total exp.: 30 min). ESO Press Photo eso0421 is a false-colour composite of all of the images obtained in B, Halpha, [OIII], 
    and [SII] where each waveband was associated to a given colour: B to blue, [OIII] to green; Halpha to orange, and [SII] to red. The field of view 
    covers 34 x 33 arcmin2. North is up and East is to the left. The images were first processed by Massimo Robberto (STSci) then further combined by 
    Hännes Heyer and Henri Boffin (ESO).</Description>
    <Target>Undefined</Target>
    <ForegroundImageSet>
      <ImageSet MSRCommunityId="0" MSRComponentId="0" Permission="0" Generic="False" DataSetType="Sky" BandPass="Visible" Url="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/eso/eso0421a/L{1}X{2}Y{3}.png" TileLevels="4" WidthFactor="2" Sparse="True" Rotation="0.08890549347008958" QuadTreeMap="" Projection="Tangent" Name="The Orion Nebula (M42)" FileType=".png" CenterY="-5.36093378445" CenterX="83.8576331954" BottomsUp="False" StockSet="False" ElevationModel="False" OffsetX="0.040804248008348004" OffsetY="-0.024657112432852034" BaseTileLevel="0" BaseDegreesPerTile="0.6536773133003565" MeanRadius="0">
        <Credits>ESO</Credits>
