  <Place MSRCommunityId="0" MSRComponentId="0" Permission="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/eso/eso1625a/thumb.jpg" Name="A deep infrared view of the Orion Nebula from HAWK-I" DataSetType="Sky" RA="5.5879371026376923" Dec="-5.3387740086782092" Constellation="ORI" Classification="Unidentified" Magnitude="0" Distance="0" ZoomLevel="3.7517026905339019" Rotation="0" Angle="0" DomeAlt="0" DomeAz="0" Opacity="100" AngularSize="3.7517026905339019">
    <Description>This spectacular image of the Orion Nebula star-formation region was obtained from multiple exposures using the HAWK-I infrared camera on ESO’s 
    Very Large Telescope in Chile. This is the deepest view ever of this region and reveals more very faint planetary-mass objects than expected.</Description>
    <Target>Undefined</Target>
